## \*\*Getting Started\*\*

Follow these steps to set up and run \*\*StuDyEaSe\*\* locally on your machine.

### \*\*Prerequisites\*\*

Ensure you have the following installed locally:

\* \*\*Node.js\*\* (v16.x or higher)
\* \*\*npm\*\* or \*\*yarn\*\* package manager
\* \*\*Git\*\*


### \*\*Installation\*\*

1. \*\*Clone the repository:\*\*

```bash
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/StuDyEaSe.git
   cd StuDyEaSe
   ```
Install dependencies:
```bash
   npm install
   genai install in terminal
   ```

Environment Configuration
Create a `.env` file in the root directory by copying the sample template:
```bash
   cp .env.example .env
   ```
Open `.env` and configure your API keys and environment variables:
```env
   PORT=5000
   AI\\\_API\\\_KEY=your\\\_actual\\\_api\\\_key\\\_here
   DATABASE\\\_URL=your\\\_database\\\_connection\\\_string
   JWT\\\_SECRET=your\\\_jwt\\\_secret\\\_key
   ```
> \\\*\\\*Warning:\\\*\\\* \\\*\\\*Never commit your actual `.env` file or API keys to a public GitHub repository.\\\*\\\*

Running the Application
Development Mode (Frontend & Backend):
```bash
  npm run dev
  ```
Production Build:
```bash
  npm run build
  npm start
  ```
Once running, open your browser and navigate to `http://localhost:3000` (or `http://localhost:5000` depending on your server setup).
