Security Considerations
API Key Protection: All external API calls (e.g., AI services) are routed through backend endpoints to prevent exposing sensitive keys on the client side.
Authentication & Auth Tokens: User authentication uses encrypted password hashing and secure token management (JWT / Session handling).
Environment Variables: Sensitive settings are stored securely in `.env` files and excluded from version control via `.gitignore`.
